InterfaceFileManager: treat the FileManager result as optional, not ErrorOr

clang's FileManager::getFile returned an ErrorOr, so tapi asks the result
for .getError().  The modern spelling, getOptionalFileRef, returns a
CustomizableOptional instead, which has no such member -- so this cannot
be handled by the mechanical renames in
mk/scripts/tapi-modernize-llvm-api.sh and needs the error handling
restructured.

readFile still has to return an Expected, so the lost error code is
replaced with the one the old path would have produced for a missing
file.  shouldWrite only tested the error to decide "not there yet", which
is exactly what the optional's own emptiness says.

Applies after mk/scripts/tapi-modernize-llvm-api.sh has renamed getFile.

--- a/lib/Core/InterfaceFileManager.cpp
+++ b/lib/Core/InterfaceFileManager.cpp
@@ -36,7 +36,8 @@
                                                 const ReadFlags flags) {
   auto file = _fm.getOptionalFileRef(path);
   if (!file)
-    return errorCodeToError(file.getError());
+    return errorCodeToError(
+        std::make_error_code(std::errc::no_such_file_or_directory));
 
   auto bufferOrErr = _fm.getBufferForFile(*file,
                                           /*RequiresNullTerminator=*/true,
@@ -68,7 +69,7 @@
                                   const InterfaceFile *file,
                                   FileType fileType) const {
   auto existingFile = _fm.getOptionalFileRef(path);
-  if (auto err = existingFile.getError())
+  if (!existingFile)
     return WriteAction::NewFile;
 
   auto bufferOrErr = _fm.getBufferForFile(*existingFile,
